<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miscellānĕus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miscill-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		miscellus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>mixed, miscellaneous</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turba,</span>”
				<i>of all sorts</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 129 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miscellānĕa</span></b> ,
			ōrum, 
			n.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A hash of different sorts of broken meat, a
				gallimaufry, hodge-podge</i>, the coarse diet of gladiators,
				<i><span class="en">Juv.
				11, 20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A writing on miscellaneous subjects</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Miscellanea Ptolemaei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Val. 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
